# Generated artifacts asserted BYTE FOR BYTE, so a formatter must not touch
# them.
#
# `golden_artifacts_match` compares the emitted bytes against these files —
# that is what makes them a regression net for the renderer that reads the
# artifact, rather than a check that the same JSON was produced in some
# formatting. prettier collapses a short array onto one line and
# `serde_json::to_vec_pretty` does not, so leaving them in scope makes the hook
# and the test disagree permanently.
#
# Regenerate with `REACHGRAPH_BLESS=1 cargo test -p reachgraph-core`, which is a
# deliberate command for the reason `cargo xtask public-api --bless` is one.
reachgraph-core/tests/golden/

# The fixture corpus is hand-written and prettier DOES own it — no entry here.

# `THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md` is GENERATED — `cargo xtask third-party-licenses`
# — and the release checklist fails when regenerating it produces a diff
# (plan-07 §6.2, §7.3). prettier reflows the tables and re-indents the
# `<details>` blocks, so with it in scope the hook and the generator disagree
# permanently and the notice can never be proved current.
#
# It is also mostly other people's words. A formatter has no business inside a
# reproduced licence text — the same argument ADR-0738 makes for the vendored
# JavaScript.
THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md
